#. max 6143 bytes
msgctxt "0"
msgid "\nAnother name for Gilgamesh.\nNot as in a \"#RUBS           Hero King#RUBEking who is a hero#REND,\"\nbut with the implication of being a \"#RUBS        King of Heroes#RUBEking over heroes#REND.\"\n\nThe story of Gilgamesh, mankind's oldest hero, was\nreplicated in the myths of countries all around the world.\nThe origin of all myths, the model heroes are based on……\nreferring to him as such would not be an exaggeration.\n\nHeroes of the various mythologies were all more or less\nderived from the legend of Gilgamesh.\nAs such, Gilgamesh possesses the prototypes of the\nNoble Phantasms those heroes carry; the original treasures\nfrom before each of their legends were arranged.\nPerhaps it's a paradox: unless Gilgamesh owns the original,\nit cannot be passed down as a Noble Phantasm\nto the heroes that were later derived from him.\n\n\n             ◆\n\nIt was a time when humanity was still few in number.\nRuling his kingdom and living in luxury as he saw fit, \ngathering all the treasures of the world into his treasury.\n\nIn that treasury held the originals\nof treasured swords that saved later heroes,\nand cursed swords that took the lives of heroes.\n\nHerein lies the reason Gilgamesh is the King of Heroes.\nOrdinarily, a hero would only have a single Noble Phantasm.\nOwning unlimited numbers of them would naturally include\nthe \"legend\" those heroes are weak against.\nIt would be impossible for the average Heroic Spirit\nto contend with him.\n\nAs a Heroic Spirit, he is absolutely indomitable\nin battle against other Heroic Spirits.\nThere may be a number of heroes who hold the title of king,\nsuch as the King of Knights and the King of Conquerors,\nbut there is only #RUBS              under heaven and earth#RUBEone man in the world#REND with the name\nof \"the absolute king of all heroes.\"\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. max 6143 bytes
msgctxt "1"
msgid "キーワード１偽名テキスト"
msgstr ""

#. max 6143 bytes
msgctxt "2"
msgid "As a young man, Gilgamesh's violent disposition only grew.\nNaturally, the people of Uruk, but even the gods\nwho dispatched him were greatly perplexed by his violence.\n\n\"Gilgamesh is not fulfilling his original purpose.\"\n\"That insolent creature needs someone to punish him―――\"\n\nWith that conclusion, the gods sent a single being\nto the surface. Their name was Enkidu.\nMade by a god and given her blood, just like Gilgamesh.\n\n             ◆\n\nThey had neither #RUBSgender#RUBEsex#REND nor a fixed form.\nShaped from clay by a god, Enkidu was \"Uruk's greatest\nweapon,\" able to change their shape at will.\n\nAccording to that#RUBS  mother's#RUBE god's#REND will,\nEnkidu confronted Gilgamesh before the Temple of Uruk.\nClashing like a storm, they fought throughout the city.\n\nAfter a fierce battle, they both collapsed to the ground,\npraised each other's valor, and became peerless friends.\n\nFor Gilgamesh, who'd been without equal, it was\nthe first time he found someone he could call \"a friend.\"\n\n             ◆\n\nAfterwards, though his egotism didn't change, Gilgamesh\nwas admonished by Enkidu and softened his tyranny.\n\nGilgamesh, who had someone who understood him in Enkidu,\ndefeated the forest guardian and beast of a god,\nHumbaba, and took possession of every treasure as\nthe greatest king on Earth.\n\nAt that time, Gilgamesh was so dazzlingly powerful,\nhe was an existence that not even the gods could\navert their eyes from.\n\nA goddess fell in love with that Gilgamesh.\nIt was the goddess of fertility, Ishtar.\nShe proposed to Gilgamesh, but he quickly refused.\nHe knew that how much Ishtar was\na whimsical and brutal witch who broke men.\n\nIshtar, enraged by Gilgamesh's insult, begged her father,\nAnu, in tears for retribution and released the greatest\nof Divine Beasts, \"the Bull of Heaven\" onto the earth.\n\n#RUBS The Bull of Heaven#RUBE\"Gugalanna#REND\" was #RUBS   a skyscraping#RUBEan extreme#REND disaster clad in storms.\nWhen it appeared, a seven-year famine and destruction\nstruck the earth. In other words, the downfall of Uruk.\n\nAgainst this unrivaled Divine Beast, Gilgamesh and Enkidu\nworked together to fight it and repelled it splendidly.\nThe goddess had lost face once again.\nNaturally, Isthar's rage hadn't calmed, so she requested\nof the gods the death for either of the two.\nFor a mortal to kill the beast of the gods was a sin.\n\nIshtar's wish was granted, and one of the two,\nEnkidu, created by the gods and unable to defy that decree,\nslowly weakened and died.\n\n……the sole person who understood that king, Enkidu.\nJust how large a shadow this loss cast over Gilgamesh\nis told in the rest of his life afterward.\n\n             ◆\n\nEnkidu was an autonomous weapon made from clay by the gods.\nIn SE.RA.PH terms, they'd be something like an AI.\nBeing complete from birth, they neither grow nor evolve.\nAble to take various forms as needed, it's said their\nusual form was of a 16-year-old, with long hair shining\na faint light-green, unable to be taken as a boy or a girl.\n"
msgstr ""

#. max 6143 bytes
msgctxt "3"
msgid "キーワード２偽名テキスト"
msgstr ""

#. max 6143 bytes
msgctxt "4"
msgid "\nGilgamesh's final Noble Phantasm, exemplifying creation―――\nthe beginning of everything.\n\nBearing the name of a god from Mesopotamian mythology,\ncausing the severance of space, the Sword of Rupture, Ea.\n\nThe god Ea is believed to be the quasi-deification of the\npower of the planet that turned, smashed, and stabilized\nthe surface of the Earth in its primordial stages,\ncovered in gas and seas of magma.\n\nMost gods began building nations after primordial Earth\nstabilized into a world that could sustain life,\nbut Ea was a god who built the planet before them.\n\nGilgamesh's sword, bearing Ea's name,\nalters space itself by agitating spacetime through\nthe rotation of three gigantic layers of force fields.\n\nIts true power is not something to be used against\na single lifeform, but against the world. Even among\nthe many Noble Phantasms possessed by Servants,\nit's one of the best; the sword \"that cut the world apart.\"\n\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. max 6143 bytes
msgctxt "5"
msgid "宝具・偽名のテキストを記述します。"
msgstr ""

#. max 6143 bytes
msgctxt "6"
msgid "\nA measure of the divine attributes in someone's body.\n\nThough he possesses the highest of Divine Spirit aptitude,\nGilgamesh himself hates the gods so its rank has decreased."
msgstr ""

#. max 6143 bytes
msgctxt "7"
msgid "スキル１偽名テキスト"
msgstr ""

#. max 6143 bytes
msgctxt "8"
msgid "\nNot the golden ratio of one's body,\nbut how much money one is destined to acquire in life.\n\nAt Rank A, it could be described as a soul of gold.\nEven while living the high life in a Goldie manner,\nhe won't ever want for money in his life."
msgstr ""

#. max 6143 bytes
msgctxt "9"
msgid "スキル２偽名テキスト"
msgstr ""

#. max 6143 bytes
msgctxt "10"
msgid "\nThe ability to acquire higher quality items.\nIt's good luck for frequently obtaining even rare items,\nbut since it only applies to Gilgamesh himself,\nit does not benefit his Master.\n\n             ◆\n\nGilgamesh is a collector of treasures.\n\"I've collected all the treasures of the earth\"\nis what Gilgamesh likes to say, but it's not a metaphor.\nHe collected, stored, and sealed away a sample of\nall the technology developed during his age.\n\nRather than just treasure, what Gilgamesh stored away\nwas \"the essence of human ingenuity\" itself.\nIf it's not in his treasury, then it's something made\n\"by a new humanity, through an entirely new concept\"\nor \"by intelligent life from another celestial body\";\none of the two.\n\nSo of course he has airplanes and submarines.\nHuman desires haven't changed#RUBS                Anno Domini, The Christian Era   #RUBE from before AD#REND, and arts\nfrom the age of magic weren't inferior to modern technology.\nPeople usually realize the \"tools of hope\" they dream of,\nand each time, it ended up confiscated by the king's hand.\n\nThe attack skill Gilgamesh uses, \"Gate of Babylon,\"\nejects the treasure he's collected like arrows.\nThe gates to the golden capital open, and his treasures\nare shot out from his treasury.\n\nAs a side note, after the Noble Phantasms shot out are used,\nthey return to his treasury no matter how far they went.\n\"Hmph. I have a Noble Phantasm that excels at retrieval,\"\nsays the person himself.\n"
msgstr ""

#. max 6143 bytes
msgctxt "11"
msgid "スキル３偽名テキスト"
msgstr ""

#. max 6143 bytes
msgctxt "12"
msgid "\nThe demigod king who governed the Sumerian city-state Uruk\nin a time before Christ. Not as a mere legend but having\ntruly existed, the king accounted in mankind's oldest epic,\n\"The Epic of Gilgamesh.\"\n\nWith great Divinity as 2/3rds god and 1/3rd human,\nhe was perfected as a transcendent being who attained\neverything in the world, without equal in the world.\n\nAs a child, he was adored by people as the ideal ruler, but\nperhaps from being seen as almighty, he grew inconsiderate\nof his subjects and he came to rule Uruk with an iron fist.\n\nHowever, simple despotism doesn't make him a tyrant;\nUruk truly prospered, he found a friend he could talk to,\nand personally subjugated monsters that threatened\nhis people, are heroic qualities that cannot be questioned.\n\nHe is the heroic figure who defeated the bull so large\nit blocked out the heavens, and rendered the civilization of \nhis fortified Sumerian city unshakeable.\n\n             ◆\n\nThe following is historical fact, not from \"The Epic.\"\nAccording to a piece of inscription found in an excavation\nof its ruins, Uruk was a city-state on the Persian Gulf in\nSouthern Mesopotamia, him as 5th king of its 1st dynasty.\nIt gained assets from sea trade and conquered Southern\nMesopotamia. He prevailed against Aga, king of the Kish,\nwho ruled the north and unified the city-states of Sumer.\nHowever, due to reckless deforestation to build ships,\ntheir agricultural land was devastated.\n\nThat's why Gilgamesh went all the way to far-off Phoenicia\n(modern Lebanon) seeking giant trees, the Cedar of Lebanon,\nfought against the resident of the woods, Humbaba,\nwon, and said to have brought back many trees with him.\n\n"
msgstr ""

#. max 6143 bytes
msgctxt "13"
msgid "設定１偽名テキスト"
msgstr ""

#. max 6143 bytes
msgctxt "14"
msgid "\nAccording to \"The Epic,\" after the loss of Enkidu,\nGilgamesh fell into depression, his previous vigor gone.\n\nGilgamesh was shocked by the fact that Enkidu,\nwhose strength had not been inferior to his own, could die.\n\nTormented by anxiety over \"death,\" he finally decided\nto set off for the underworld in search of immortality.\n\nIt was said there was once a sage who'd survived by putting\nmany animals on an ark before a deluge assailed the Earth.\n\nThis sage was said to be the only one on Earth\nto escape from death and live on to the present.\nSeeking him, Gilgamesh set off to the wilderness alone.\n\nAt the end of that long journey, through many hardships,\nGilgamesh finally arrived at the underworld.\nThere, he met the sage named Utnapishtim, spoke with him,\nand finally obtained the Herb of Immortality.\n\nGilgamesh was to transcend the \"death\" that had\ntaken even Enkidu.\n\n             ◆\n\nHis heart's desire fulfilled, on his way back to Uruk,\nGilgamesh stopped by a spring. He cleansed himself;\napparently intending to test it in perfect condition.\n\nHowever.\nAs he was bathing, a hungry snake\nhappened to smell the Herb of Immortality.\n\nBy the time he noticed, it was too late.\nWhen Gilgamesh emerged from the spring in a panic,\nall that remained was the skin that snake had shed.\n\nHaving lost the Herb of Immortality,\nGilgamesh was irritated for a long time,\nbut he made his way back to his castle in Uruk.\n\nAfter this, while strict, he ruled his state quietly,\nentrusted it to the next king and went to his eternal rest.\n\nWithout telling anyone the Herb of Immortality's location.\n\n             ◆\n\nMankind's oldest King of Heroes, Gilgamesh.\nDiscord with the gods, the quest for immortality,\na deluge that enveloped the world.\nIn that epic was the basis of every legend.\n\nThe truth of this epic, with many of its finer details\nuncertain, now lies across the veil of romance.\n\nAs another side note, the reason snakes are reborn with\na new body every time it sheds its skin is because it\nstole and ate Gilgamesh's herb…… or so they say.\nApparently, the way snakes live appeared to the ancients\nas a kind of immortality that was unavailable to humans.\n\n"
msgstr ""

